If a patient has a gastrointestinal-comorbidity and does not have a current-gastrointestinal-bleeding and does not have a previous-gastrointestinal-bleeding then every clinician may use a cyclooxygenase-2-inhibitor for the patient during a gastrointestinal-risk-minimization.
If a patient has a gastrointestinal-comorbidity and does not have a current-gastrointestinal-bleeding and does not have a previous-gastrointestinal-bleeding then every clinician may use an NSAID with a proton-pump-inhibitor for the patient during a gastrointestinal-risk-minimization.
